<codeline lineno="8"><highlight class="comment"><sp/>*<sp/>The<sp/>`TopMatching`<sp/>class,<sp/>implemented<sp/>in<sp/>Cython,<sp/>is<sp/>a<sp/>specialized<sp/>selection<sp/>template<sp/>within<sp/>the<sp/>AnalysisG<sp/>framework,<sp/>designed<sp/>for<sp/>analyzing<sp/>top<sp/>quark<sp/>matching<sp/>in<sp/>Monte<sp/>Carlo<sp/>20<sp/>(MC20)<sp/>events.<sp/>It<sp/>inherits<sp/>from<sp/>the<sp/>generic<sp/>`SelectionTemplate`<sp/>class,<sp/>extending<sp/>its<sp/>functionalities<sp/>to<sp/>incorporate<sp/>specific<sp/>criteria<sp/>for<sp/>matching<sp/>top<sp/>quarks,<sp/>particularly<sp/>with<sp/>respect<sp/>to<sp/>energy<sp/>limits.<sp/>This<sp/>class<sp/>provides<sp/>a<sp/>high-performance<sp/>interface<sp/>to<sp/>an<sp/>underlying<sp/>C++<sp/>matching<sp/>object,<sp/>enabling<sp/>efficient<sp/>filtering<sp/>and<sp/>analysis<sp/>based<sp/>on<sp/>top<sp/>quark<sp/>matching<sp/>properties.</highlight></codeline>
